# Backend and API rules

- Validate and normalize all external input at the boundary.
- Authenticate first, then authorize access to the specific resource and action.
- Keep transport/controller code thin; place business rules in testable services or domain modules.
- Return stable, documented error codes and avoid leaking internal details.
- Make writes idempotent where retries are possible.
- Use transactions when multiple writes must succeed or fail together.
- Add timeouts, cancellation, bounded retries, and backoff for external calls where appropriate.
- Emit structured logs and useful correlation identifiers without logging secrets or sensitive payloads.
- Define pagination, filtering, ordering, rate limits, and maximum payload sizes for collection endpoints.
- Update API schemas, clients, and contract tests together.
